From: GapKeep <noreply@gapkeep.org>
Subject: sysinit: the loaded data ends with .data when .tdata is empty

0012 hands GapKeep the initialised data as loaded, from __data_start to
__tdata_end, for the kernel's hash of its own image. But .tdata starts
8-byte aligned: when it is empty (GapKeep has no thread-local data) and
.data ends on a word that is not a multiple of 8, __tdata_end is 4 bytes
past the end of kernel.img, and the hash covered 4 bytes the file doesn't
have (tests/check_kernel_hash.sh caught it when .data grew by a word).

- circle.ld: __data_end, the end of .data.
- sysinit(): the data ends at __tdata_end if .tdata has anything in it,
  otherwise at __data_end.

--- a/circle.ld
+++ b/circle.ld
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@
 
 	.data : {
 		*(.data*)
+		__data_end = .;		/* gapkeep: where kernel.img ends without .tdata */
 	}
 
 	.tdata : ALIGN(8) {
--- a/lib/sysinit.cpp
+++ b/lib/sysinit.cpp
@@ -348,9 +348,14 @@
 	// anything changes them, for the kernel's hash of its own image
 	if (sysinit_data_loaded != 0)
 	{
+		// the image ends with .tdata if it has any, otherwise with .data:
+		// an empty .tdata starts 8-byte aligned, which may be past the end
 		extern unsigned char __data_start;
+		extern unsigned char __data_end;
+		extern unsigned char __tdata_start;
 		extern unsigned char __tdata_end;
-		sysinit_data_loaded (&__data_start, &__tdata_end - &__data_start);
+		unsigned char *pEnd = &__tdata_end > &__tdata_start ? &__tdata_end : &__data_end;
+		sysinit_data_loaded (&__data_start, pEnd - &__data_start);
 	}
 
 	// halt, if KERNEL_MAX_SIZE is not properly set
